  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ion Implantation">
  <data key="d0">Ion Implantation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Ion implantation is a process in semiconductor manufacturing that introduces impurities into specific regions to form P-type or N-type areas.&lt;SEP&gt;Ion Implantation is a technique used to introduce impurities into the silicon wafer to modify its electrical properties.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ae080121232af020ad6ba3a6ec2d7d3f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ef94f588ef70d0bd8967e7353481a56</data>
  <data key="d4">半导体材料介绍.txt&lt;SEP&gt;集成电路制造工艺.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1770983003</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Deposition">
  <data key="d0">Deposition</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Deposition is a process in semiconductor manufacturing that forms metal interconnects or insulating layers on the wafer.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ae080121232af020ad6ba3a6ec2d7d3f</data>
  <data key="d4">半导体材料介绍.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1770982433</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Packaging &amp; Testing">
  <data key="d0">Packaging &amp; Testing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Packaging and testing are the final steps in semiconductor manufacturing, where the wafer is cut into individual chips, packaged, and tested for electrical performance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ae080121232af020ad6ba3a6ec2d7d3f</data>
  <data key="d4">半导体材料介绍.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1770982433</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Semiconductor Device">
  <data key="d0">Semiconductor Device</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A semiconductor device is a type of electronic component that utilizes the properties of semiconductor materials, such as diodes, transistors, and integrated circuits.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ae080121232af020ad6ba3a6ec2d7d3f</data>
  <data key="d4">半导体材料介绍.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1770982433</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Semiconductor Manufacturing">
  <data key="d0">Semiconductor Manufacturing</data>
  <data key="d1">process</data>
  <data key="d2">Semiconductor manufacturing is the process of creating semiconductor devices, involving steps like wafer preparation, oxidation, lithography, etching, ion implantation, deposition, and packaging and testing.&lt;SEP&gt;Semiconductor Manufacturing encompasses all steps from wafer preparation to final testing and packaging.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ae080121232af020ad6ba3a6ec2d7d3f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29d2df4d26a3885b820e69482a2d3ea7</data>
  <data key="d4">半导体材料介绍.txt&lt;SEP&gt;集成电路制造工艺.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1770983002</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CMP Technology">
  <data key="d0">CMP Technology</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">CMP Technology is a critical process used to polish the surface of wafers for multi-layer metal interconnects in modern chips.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-29d2df4d26a3885b820e69482a2d3ea7</data>
  <data key="d4">集成电路制造工艺.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1770983001</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Metalization">
  <data key="d0">Metalization</data>
  <data key="d1">process</data>
  <data key="d2">Metalization is the process of creating electrical connections using copper or aluminum in semiconductor manufacturing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-29d2df4d26a3885b820e69482a2d3ea7</data>
  <data key="d4">集成电路制造工艺.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1770983001</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Back-End-of-Line (BEOL)">
  <data key="d0">Back-End-of-Line (BEOL)</data>
  <data key="d1">process</data>
  <data key="d2">BEOL refers to the later stages of semiconductor manufacturing that involve connecting transistors into circuits.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-29d2df4d26a3885b820e69482a2d3ea7</data>
  <data key="d4">集成电路制造工艺.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1770983001</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Wafer Sort (CP)">
  <data key="d0">Wafer Sort (CP)</data>
  <data key="d1">process</data>
  <data key="d2">Wafer Sort is the testing phase where each chip on a wafer is electrically tested and defective chips are marked.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-29d2df4d26a3885b820e69482a2d3ea7</data>
  <data key="d4">集成电路制造工艺.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1770983001</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dicing">
  <data key="d0">Dicing</data>
  <data key="d1">process</data>
  <data key="d2">Dicing is the process of cutting a wafer into individual chips (Dies).</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-29d2df4d26a3885b820e69482a2d3ea7</data>
  <data key="d4">集成电路制造工艺.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1770983001</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Packaging">
  <data key="d0">Packaging</data>
  <data key="d1">process</data>
  <data key="d2">Packaging involves securing the chip on a substrate, connecting its pins, and protecting it with materials like epoxy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-29d2df4d26a3885b820e69482a2d3ea7</data>
  <data key="d4">集成电路制造工艺.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1770983001</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Final Test (FT)">
  <data key="d0">Final Test (FT)</data>
  <data key="d1">process</data>
  <data key="d2">Final Test is the comprehensive testing of packaged chips for functionality and environmental performance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-29d2df4d26a3885b820e69482a2d3ea7</data>
  <data key="d4">集成电路制造工艺.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1770983001</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Photoresist">
  <data key="d0">Photoresist</data>
  <data key="d1">material</data>
  <data key="d2">Photoresist is a light-sensitive organic material used in photolithography, available in positive and negative types.&lt;SEP&gt;Photoresist is a light-sensitive material used in photolithography to transfer circuit patterns onto the wafer.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-29d2df4d26a3885b820e69482a2d3ea7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ef94f588ef70d0bd8967e7353481a56</data>
